    "issued": "2026-09-29",
    "note": "Transcribed by hand from the INPI's two lists — the recognised indications of provenance (Indicação de Procedência, IP; up to 29 September 2026) and the recognised denominations of origin (Denominação de Origem, DO; up to 23 June 2026) — keeping the Brazilian ones whose product is wine: each geographical name as the list writes it, its kind, its number, the product as written, the date of registration (and of any change the list gives), the state, and the municipalities its delimitation names. \"Santa Catarina\" is the list's geographical name for the indication its delimitation calls the \"Vinhos de Altitude de Santa Catarina\". Vale dos Vinhedos is in both lists, an IP since 2002 and a DO since 2012; Vales da Uva Goethe, an IP from 2012, became a DO on 10 June 2025. Pinto Bandeira's IP lay in the municipalities of Bento Gonçalves and Farroupilha when it was registered (2010). Official acts have no copyright in Brazil (Lei 9.610/1998, art. 8, IV). The date shown is when a name took its present kind: Vales da Uva Goethe's as a DO (10 June 2025), its first registration as an IP kept as firstRegisteredOn. Monte Belo and Santa Catarina are placed only amid their municipalities: OpenStreetMap's Monte Belo is another place, in the north-west of Rio Grande do Sul, and its Santa Catarina the whole state. Vale dos Vinhedos's article on the Portuguese Wikipedia (Wikidata Q1241994) describes the denomination's page; the indication of provenance of the same name takes no article, as one text on two pages would be dropped.",
    "urlDenominations": "https://www.gov.br/inpi/pt-br/servicos/indicacoes-geograficas/arquivos/status-pedidos/LISTACOMASDENOMINAESDEORIGEMRECONHECIDAS.At23Junho2026.pdf",
